 [17592186307487 1034 "6" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534749 true] [17592186307487 1111 #uuid "462a6887-412c-52bf-86ac-83acb83ecabc" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307488 1034 "4" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534749 true] [17592186307488 1111 #uuid "0facf9e9-db65-5483-b86f-15db2510e3f6" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307489 1034 "5" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534749 true] [17592186307489 1111 #uuid "f00a979b-a094-584c-ae99-98695213eb82" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307490 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307491 13194139534749 true] [17592186307490 1089 "q-162348" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307490 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534749 true] [17592186307490 1100 "Let $z$ and $w$ be $8$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${z}^{8}=1$\n- $(zw)^{8}=1$\n- $zw$ is an $8$th root of unity" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307490 1113 #uuid "0f7810dd-0a09-524f-951a-0d2c3a074300" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307490 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, if $z$ and $w$ are $8$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{8}={w}^{8}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{8} & ={z}^{8}{w}^{8} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that $(zw)^{8}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is an $8$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307492 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307493 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307494 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307495 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307496 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1041 "selection" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307492 13194139534749 true] [17592186307491 1110 #uuid "357a5205-43f7-5d16-98cf-4ab3625f6824" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307492 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307492 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307492 1111 #uuid "4e9d13c7-2257-5ff4-8d39-10d6822f1af4" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307493 1034 "I only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307493 1111 #uuid "32a83d77-8732-5751-bde8-f6c84d0b9124" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307494 1034 "III only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307494 1111 #uuid "ca29964d-1616-5f23-a104-40bc51491797" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307495 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307495 1111 #uuid "1fcdfcf2-4205-5072-908f-afe82f93e58c" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307496 1034 "II only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307496 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307496 1111 #uuid "f2bc3de5-7430-56cb-a216-0a2bb15e07fe" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307497 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307498 13194139534749 true] [17592186307497 1089 "q-162349" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307497 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534749 true] [17592186307497 1100 "Let $z$ be an $8$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $({z}^{4})^{2}=-1$\n- ${z}^{4}$ is an $8$th root of unity\n- ${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307497 1113 #uuid "4d7cd035-57ca-527d-99bf-083560e8300a" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307497 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({z}^{4})}^{2}={z}^{8}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{4})^{8} & =({z}^{8})^{4} \\\\  & =(1)^{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{4}$ is a $8$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement I, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{4})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307499 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307500 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307501 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307502 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307503 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1041 "selection" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307499 13194139534749 true] [17592186307498 1110 #uuid "5a4872cd-662c-5c19-95ba-1a88838a9570" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307499 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307499 1111 #uuid "b075c6f4-19e6-5c85-b7f4-f6b087e304aa" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307500 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307500 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307500 1111 #uuid "ca34f3cd-3d05-5f6d-9560-fa62d13c314a" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307501 1034 "I only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307501 1111 #uuid "4b45f471-e6cf-569e-b3b2-ce2297122572" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307502 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307502 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307502 1111 #uuid "5650b7bf-2ff8-542e-a64f-2afe98f40fd8" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307503 1034 "II only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307503 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307503 1111 #uuid "b4bdbbc7-9a89-561c-bd4a-19f1cc7cd01c" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307504 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307505 13194139534749 true] [17592186307504 1089 "q-162350" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307504 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534749 true] [17592186307504 1100 "Let $z$ and $w$ be $4$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${z}^{4}=-1$\n- $(zw)^{4}=0$\n- $zw$ is a $4$th root of unity" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307504 1113 #uuid "9f713879-94e6-5f37-9fb5-ef877febabbd" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307504 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ and $w$ are $4$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{4}={w}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{4} & ={z}^{4}{w}^{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have seen above that $(zw)^{4}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is a $4$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307506 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307507 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307508 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307509 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307510 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1041 "selection" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307508 13194139534749 true] [17592186307505 1110 #uuid "0d516f43-a53a-5694-9677-25aa51fd0430" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307506 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307506 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307506 1111 #uuid "0e8a7c7b-84fa-56e2-82b0-e09f7bdfff81" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307507 1