3-5774-5ec4-856c-c4767abb46c0" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307518 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,  since $z$ and $w$ are $6$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have\n\n$$\n{z}^{6}={w}^{6}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\nz{w}^{6}=z\\cdot 1=z\\ne w.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{6} & ={z}^{6}{w}^{6} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have seen above that $(zw)^{6}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is a $6$th root of unity.  \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II  only.\"" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307520 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307521 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307522 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307523 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307524 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1041 "selection" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307524 13194139534749 true] [17592186307519 1110 #uuid "7eee9821-fdb4-5441-89f4-d91ab707113b" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307520 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307520 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307520 1111 #uuid "e04279c5-fcc5-57ca-b61e-6452963bf41c" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307521 1034 "I only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307521 1111 #uuid "48f2a665-e176-55f3-8975-da2ac6706e8f" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307522 1034 "III only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307522 1111 #uuid "ff2e1615-3c19-5795-8007-293a17c020bc" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307523 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307523 1111 #uuid "2370cbf5-52f3-5212-bd6b-1451833a9745" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307524 1034 "II only" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534749 true] [17592186307524 1111 #uuid "30d6ecd3-ac51-5646-b8e4-41226413c83b" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307525 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307526 13194139534749 true] [17592186307525 1089 "q-319728" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307525 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534749 true] [17592186307525 1100 "The $4$th root of unity ${e}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/2}$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{e}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/2}={z}^{p},\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ is the principal $4$th root of unity. What is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307525 1113 #uuid "74fc853a-fded-57a5-a2b5-a1007937b0be" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307525 1145 "Recall that the $4$th roots of unity can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}/4}\n$$\n\nwhere $k=0,1,2,3.$ \n\nWe obtain the *principal* $4$th root of unity by substituting $k=1:$\n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi \\text{i}/4}={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2}\n$$\n\nWe can write the given root of unity as a power of the principal root as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/2} & =({e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2})^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=3.$" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307526 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307527 13194139534749 true] [17592186307526 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534749 true] [17592186307526 1041 "field-1" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307526 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307527 13194139534749 true] [17592186307526 1110 #uuid "4043f3f6-ef5f-5e57-998e-489b97a8a68d" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307527 1034 "3" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534749 true] [17592186307527 1111 #uuid "ccdf531f-fdc2-526b-8155-0d71eeda4828" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307528 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307529 13194139534749 true] [17592186307528 1089 "q-319729" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307528 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534749 true] [17592186307528 1100 "The $6$th root of unity ${e}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{e}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}={z}^{p},\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ is the principal $6$th root of unity. What is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307528 1113 #uuid "eb228e5e-6fac-55e4-8bf0-6272a0da3e87" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307528 1145 "Recall that the $6$th roots of unity can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}/6}\n$$\n\nwhere $k=0,1,…,5.$ \n\nWe obtain the *principal* $6$th root of unity by substituting $k=1:$\n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi \\text{i}/6}={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}\n$$\n\nWe can write the given root of unity as a power of the principal root as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3} & =({e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3})^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=4.$" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307530 13194139534749 true] [17592186307529 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534749 true] [17592186307529 1041 "field-1" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307529 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307530 13194139534749 true] [17592186307529 1110 #uuid "ec3162c1-4c42-5e6f-bad3-db9d68f026a8" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307530 1034 "4" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534749 true] [17592186307530 1111 #uuid "c0cc555f-45d1-566e-95d1-53d2ac7b726c" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307531 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307532 13194139534749 true] [17592186307531 1089 "q-319735" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307531 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534749 true] [17592186307531 1100 "The $13$th root of unity ${e}^{22\\pi \\text{i}/13}$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{e}^{22\\pi \\text{i}/13}={z}^{p},\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ is the principal $13$th root of unity. What is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307531 1113 #uuid "466795ee-3584-581f-9a08-c993f5d79171" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307531 1145 "Recall that the $13$th roots of unity can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}/13}\n$$\n\nwhere $k=0,1,…,12.$ \n\nWe obtain the *principal* $13$th root of unity by substituting $k=1:$\n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi \\text{i}/13}={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/13}\n$$\n\nWe can write the given root of unity as a power of the principal root as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{22\\pi \\text{i}/13} & =({e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/13})^{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=11.$" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307533 13194139534749 true] [17592186307532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307534 13194139534749 true] [17592186307532 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534749 true] [17592186307532 1041 "field-1" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307532 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307534 13194139534749 true] [17592186307532 1110 #uuid "9c5b861b-e743-5565-959e-058e41e335a0" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307533 1034 "22" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534749 true] [17592186307533 1111 #uuid "641ebac1-accc-5ef7-8a01-64cf1ae8fd48" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307534 1034 "11" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534749 true] [17592186307534 1111 #uuid "744d350a-52d8-573a-a5ef-a00682a83b10" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307535 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307536 13194139534749 true] [17592186307535 1089 "q-319750" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307535 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534749 true] [17592186307535 1100 "The sum of all twelve $12$th roots of unity is equal to$\\,$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534749 true] [17592186307535 1113 #uuid "21aa80e5-d034-5d1d-8759-9490ca9161a9" 13194139534749 true] [17592186307535 1145 "Recall that the principal $12$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/12}\\ne 1,\n$$\n\nand that any $12$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,…,11.$  Also, we have ${z}^{12}=1.$\n\nUsing the 